# Pulse Web SDK Structure

Keep module layout consistent and predictable.

## Folder Placement Rules

- Put reusable type/interface definitions in `pulse-web-otel/src/types/`.
- For domain-specific shared types, create a subfolder under `src/types/` (example: `src/types/interactions/`).
- Put reusable pure helper functions in `pulse-web-otel/src/utils/`.
- For domain-specific helpers, create a subfolder under `src/utils/` (example: `src/utils/interactions/`).
- Put constants in `pulse-web-otel/src/constants/`.
- For domain-specific constants, create a subfolder under `src/constants/` (example: `src/constants/interactions/`).

## Do Not

- Do not create ad-hoc `types/`, `utils/`, or `constants/` folders nested inside feature folders when an equivalent `src/types|utils|constants` path exists.
- Do not mix runtime logic with declaration-only types/interfaces in the same file unless tightly coupled and local-only.

## Feature Modules

- Keep feature orchestrators/state machines in their feature folder (for example `src/interactions/`).
- Import shared types/utilities/constants from the global structured folders.
